# End-of-line handling.
#
# Upstream RefindPlus stores most files with CRLF in the repository, but a few
# files (Main/menu.c and .gitignore) are stored with LF. These two rules keep
# the LF-stored files normalized to LF in the repository, so they stay
# byte-identical to upstream and never produce whole-file diffs or merge
# conflicts.
#
# "text" (without "eol") means:
#   - the index (repository) always stores LF
#   - the working tree keeps native line endings (CRLF on Windows, via
#     core.eol), so nothing on disk changes
#
# Files that upstream stores with CRLF are deliberately left unlisted so their
# repository content continues to match upstream exactly.

Main/menu.c    text
.gitignore     text

# Keep this file itself as LF on disk.
.gitattributes text eol=lf
